{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["<b>You have declared … He has declared you.</b> They have no supporting witness in Scripture. It appears to me that it is a term of separation and distinction — you separated yourself from the gods of the nations to be for yourself an Elohim, and He separated you to Himself from the peoples of the earth to be for Him a treasured people. And I find for them a witness — it is a term of exaltation, as in ״יִתְאַמְּרוּ כָּל פֹּעֲלֵי אָוֶן״ (Psalms 94)."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 26, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:48:27.914514807Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}